    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1811">

                <pb facs="1462" n="1346" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/28a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of the Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor, in pursuance of instructions that I have received from the
                    President, to request you to be good enough to despatch two vessels with the
                    least possible delay to the ports of Beirut and <pb facs="1463" n="1347"
                        xml:id="pg1347"/> Smyrna to protect or to give refuge to American citizens
                    in case of antiforeign outbreaks there, subject, however, to any supplemental
                    requests the American Embassy at Constantinople may make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Approved. <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Taft.</hi>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
